 "relevance_note": "Single case report of a man with a GFAP variant: 'a known pathogenic DNA sequence variant within the glial fibrillary acidic protein gene, confirming adult-onset Alexander disease'.",
 "method_note": "Hand-extracted from a one-paragraph Teaching Video NeuroImages case report; a short script only assembled the JSON. The Markdown renders the '>' arrows as ' . ' ('C . T', 'arginine . cysteine'); the variant string is quoted as printed in the Markdown, no c./p. HGVS is printed, and no transcript, zygosity, inheritance or variant class is stated. The gene is printed only as the full name 'glial fibrillary acidic protein gene', recorded as printed. 'adult-onset' (from 'adult-onset Alexander disease') is recorded as the age-at-onset text; no numeric onset age is given ('several-year history'). Age 67 is the age at presentation, recorded as last evaluation; no age at diagnosis is stated. 'Did not have corticospinal tract signs' recorded as excluded for the checklist item 'spasticity or pyramidal signs' (corticospinal tract signs = pyramidal signs). Hypertrophic olivary degeneration on T2-weighted MRI is recorded as observed for 'medulla or cervical spinal cord atrophy or signal abnormality' (the inferior olive lies in the medulla; the paper does not use the word medulla). No contradictions found.",
